"notes": "City, GAAP. Governmental receipts/disbursements from Total Governmental Funds column (p7); beginning fund balance is as originally reported 2,834,973 with restatement -58,569 as an adjustment (restated 2,776,404). Check: 2,834,973 + 1,665,763 - 1,579,816 + 100,000 - 58,569 = 2,962,351. Loan collections (159,024) kept as a receipt with category other (review). Ending_cash is Cash and cash equivalents from the governmental funds Balance Sheet total column (p5); certificates of deposit 270,332 shown as ending_investments; county treasurer cash 58,448 not included. beginning_cash not shown. Business-type from Statement of Revenues, Expenses, and Changes in Net Position (p10-11) total enterprise column: no single printed total revenues/expenses, so totals computed (receipts = operating revenues + interest income + grant income + city sales tax; disbursements = operating expenses + interest expense + loss from joint venture 75,974, treated as an expense). Net position beginning as originally reported 9,499,527 plus restatement 58,569; transfers net -100,000. Check: 9,499,527 + 4,923,913 - 4,402,787 - 100,000 + 58,569 = 9,979,222. Internal service fund column (governmental activities, not in enterprise totals) ignored. Proprietary cash flow totals from p13 (total enterprise column). Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (due from/to other funds nets to zero, omitted). Detail: General Fund recorded from the departmental combining schedule (p19-20, 9 departments, GAAP basis ties to 991,283/973,612); the General Fund budgetary comparison (p14, budgetary basis, includes budget amounts) was not recorded to avoid double counting. Street and LB840 recorded from their budgetary comparison schedules (budgetary basis; actuals differ slightly from GAAP statement, see Note A on p18); CDBG schedule (p17) has no actual activity, so omitted. Operating expenses and capital outlay by department have no object breakdown, so detail_category not itemized. Read pages 1-20 of 20."
